# Phase 6: Calibration + Integration Testing

## Overview

End-to-end calibration: tune dimension weights, query limits, confidence thresholds, satiation criteria. Integration tests verifying the full pipeline from big question to synthesized answer.

## Requirements

- Functional: Calibrate default dimension weights from test queries
- Functional: Tune satiation thresholds (when to stop querying)
- Functional: Integration test: /think produces answer with ≥80% LOCAL content
- Functional: Integration test: Stage0 Step 1.5 enriches case without blocking
- Non-functional: Calibration config stored in JSON (editable without code changes)

## Related Code Files

- Create: `.claude/lib/intelligence/decomposition/calibration_config.py`
- Create: `.claude/lib/intelligence/decomposition/tests/test_integration.py`
- Modify: `.claude/lib/intelligence/decomposition/decomposer.py` — load calibration
- Read: `.claude/lib/intelligence/hunger/calibration_config.py` — reuse pattern

## Implementation Steps

1. Create `calibration_config.py`:
   - Reuse pattern from hunger engine's CalibrationConfig
   - Settings: max_queries_per_dimension (3-5), max_total_queries (40), min_confidence_threshold (0.5), satiation_coverage (0.9), cache_freshness_days (180), weight_evolution_cap (0.1)
   - Load/save from `.claude/data/decomposition/calibration.json`

2. Create `tests/test_integration.py`:
   - Test 1: Full /think pipeline with mock LLM → verify ≥10 facts stored
   - Test 2: Stage0 bridge with mock case → verify case enriched
   - Test 3: Compound learning — run same topic twice → verify fewer queries second time
   - Test 4: Template evolution — run 5 times → verify weights changed
   - Test 5: Zone tag distribution — verify [K]/[T]/[?] counts in output
   - Test 6: Satiation — verify decomposition stops when coverage ≥0.9
   - Test 7: Error resilience — LLM returns garbage → verify graceful degradation
   - Target: 10+ integration tests

3. Calibrate defaults:
   - Run test queries against mock LLM: "How to build a VC fund?", "SaaS vs agency?", "Coffee export margins?"
   - Measure: facts_per_query, parse_success_rate, useful_fact_rate
   - Adjust default weights in dimension_registry based on yield data
   - Document calibration results in plan notes

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Calibration config loads from JSON
- [ ] Integration tests verify full pipeline (10+)
- [ ] ≥80% of synthesis content from LOCAL computation
- [ ] ≤20% LLM usage (micro-fact retrieval only)
- [ ] Compound cache hit rate >30% on second similar query
- [ ] Template evolution changes weights after 5+ runs
- [ ] All tests pass

## Risk Assessment

- Default calibration too aggressive (too many queries) → mitigation: conservative defaults, tune from real usage
- Integration tests fragile due to mock quality → mitigation: realistic mock responses based on actual LLM output patterns
